// Same "next weapon hit gets a bonus, consumed on attack" shape as
// `evocation/blinding_smite.ron` -- `SelfBuff` + `buff_cat: RemoveOnAttack`,
// `duration: None` (consumed rather than timed out). Modeled with
// `BuffKind::BrandingSmite` ("Causes the wielder's next weapon hit to deal
// additional damage, no secondary effect") since no existing Smite variant
// grants an evasion-penalty rider on the struck target (checked every
// `*Smite` kind's doc comment in `common/src/comp/buff.rs` -- `Blinding`/
// `Searing`/`Staggering`/`Thunderous`/`Wrathful` each pair the bonus damage
// with a *different* specific rider, none of them "target becomes easier to
// hit"). The sheet's "foe glows, easier to hit" rider is dropped rather than
// substituted with a mismatched Smite kind.
// Same level (2), same buff kind, same shape, same energy_cost as the
// already-shipped `evocation/branding_smite.ron` -- strength matched to its
// 7.0 exactly rather than picked independently, since an apples-to-apples
// same-kind/same-level comparison exists to calibrate against directly.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.1,
    cast_duration: 0.1,
    recover_duration: 0.1,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(kind: BrandingSmite, data: BuffData(strength: 7.0, duration: None)),
    ],
    buff_cat: Some(RemoveOnAttack),
    energy_cost: 15,
    enforced_limit: true,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Transmutation),
        source: Some(Divine),
        // level 2 spell -> min_level 12, same `level * 6` convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(12)),
    ),
)
